---
title "Install GitHub CLI (intent playbook)"
---

= Install gh

Same file on every OS. PlayTime asks the Equivalence Engine for a
`cli.install` command that this computer can run. No bash-to-pwsh rewrite.

Need a catalog: `--catalog examples/fixture-catalog.sdl` or
`SCRIPTBOOK_CATALOG` pointing at `equivalence-rules-cli/catalog/tools.sdl`.

If several formats fit, pass `--format nix` (or `winget`, `deb`, …).

::: playbook [id="install-gh" shell="auto"]

::: choose [id="pkg-format" prompt="How should we install gh?" intent="cli.install" tool="gh"]
:::

::: step [id="install" intent="cli.install" tool="gh" bind="pkg-format" confirm=true]
:::

::: step [id="desktop-file" when-answer="pkg-format=appimage"]
```
echo "AppImage satellite step — skipped unless the chosen format is appimage"
```
:::

::: step [id="verify" when="install"]
```
gh --version
```
:::

:::
